    native_build_nested_replace_method_resolution_2026-07-26, 2, "closed-obsolete 2026-11-10 (p2 fix lane, release/1.0.0): premise no longer holds. (1) Pure-Simple 50.mir lowers every nested/chained .replace shape (direct chain, nested call argument, titles.push argument, call-result receiver, string interpolation, trim().replace(), replace().len(), replace().trim() argument) to two rt_string_replace calls with an Opaque(str) text-typed intermediate and zero diagnostics -- test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/nested_replace_chain_lowering_spec.spl 8/8 green on the unmodified tree; the only red seen was a spec-side type check that expected Ptr(I8) instead of the Opaque(str) text handle. (2) The filed diagnostic text exists only in the Rust seed interpreter nested-dispatch fallback (src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/interpreter_helpers/method_dispatch.rs:996) whose temporary-receiver table already lists replace (interp_chained_replace_2026-07-05 fix) -- test/01_unit/lib/common/text_nested_replace_chain_spec.spl 8/8 green on the interpreter. (3) The bug doc itself records that no isolated repro ever reproduced; the only evidence was a rotated macOS stage4 WM Vulkan gate log. Both specs are kept as regression guards; re-open only with a concrete repro from the macOS gate graph."

